<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rao Bika</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1438">1438</a>–<a href="/years/1504">1504</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rao Bika was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore</a> prince, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rao-jodha">Rao Jodha</a> of Marwar, who founded the kingdom and city of Bikaner. In 1465 he led followers north into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jangladesh">Jangladesh</a> region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thar-desert">Thar Desert</a> and won lands from Jat and Bhati chiefs. He founded Bikaner in 1488, and his descendants ruled it until the princely state joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rao-bika.jpg" alt="Rao Bika" width="320" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Narook · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rao_Bika%27s_Conquest_of_Jangladesh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
